  data:  # 100b
    kind: invariant  # 100b
    title: "The WI-nurun confidence band flags every corroborated edge: 109,622 cross_field|info on a scip-enabled self-map"  # 100b
    status: violated  # 100b
    priority: 1  # 100b
    parent:  # 100b
    tags:  # 100b
    - multi_fidelity  # 100b
    - validation  # 100b
    - scip  # 100b
    isbefore: []  # 100b
    duplicate_of: []  # 100b
    not_duplicate_of: []  # 100b
    pr_ref:  # 100b
    description: "FOUND 2026-10-20 building a scip-python-enabled self-map for WI-losig (the first time the backend ran on a real tree, after WI-nijod).\n\nFACTS. With HYPERGUMBO_SCIP_PYTHON=1, the merge pass corroborates 109,622 edges the ast-python arm and the scip arm both produced: origin [python, scip], confidence_source 'corroborated', confidence 0.95 (CORROBORATED_CONFIDENCE, ADR-0057 s5/s13), evidence_type kept as the incumbent's (ast_call_direct 67,471; ast_call 35,227; ast_name_read 6,924). spec_validator's WI-nurun band check reports EVERY one as cross_field|info \"Edge.confidence 0.95 for evidence_type 'ast_call_direct' is outside the derived band [0.5, 0.85] -- the per-emitter value no longer tracks the inference pathway\". All 109,622 flagged edges are confidence_source=corroborated (counted).\n\nWHY THE VALIDATOR IS THE WRONG SIDE. ir.py's confidence_source docstring: corroborated means two DISTINCT pathways reached the edge, \"so confidence is the declared corroboration level ... not either producer's value\". The band describes ONE pathway's value; a corroborated confidence is by definition not on it. The level is configurable ([merge] corroborated_confidence), so the validator cannot pin it to the constant either.\n\nCONSEQUENCE. scripts/check-self-tree-validation on that map: exit 1, \"cross_field|info: 109622 > baseline 0\". The ratchet is shrink-only, so WI-losig (backend-enabled CI self-map) cannot land on the shared map until this is fixed. Every user who opts in to the backend also gets ~110k spurious info violations in validation_report.\n\nFIX: the band check skips an edge whose confidence_source is corroborated."  # 100b
    fields:  # 100b
      statement: "The spec validator's per-evidence_type confidence band applies only to a confidence that came from that pathway; an edge whose confidence_source is corroborated is not judged against it."  # 100b
      root_cause: "spec_validator's band check predates corroboration (ADR-0057 s13) and checks every edge with an evidence_type and a confidence, regardless of confidence_source."  # 100b
